<!--Post: 7746--><!--Time: 1108671920-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7746"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jilleng<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jilleng<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Someone made the comment that a seriel killer doesn&#39;t usually stop killing...BTK may have been moving around the states throught the last 20 years and leaving dead bodies in his wake...he may have now made full circle back to KS...here&#39;s the link for anybody wantint to review some of the U.S. cold case files to see if his MO fits any of the crimes. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.coldcasecenter.com/cold_cases.htm" target=_top>http://www.coldcasecenter.com/cold_cases.htm</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7746-->
<!--Post: 8746--><!--Time: 1109305032-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8746"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 8:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.doenetwork.us" target=_top>www.doenetwork.us</a> <BR><a href="http://www.forthelost.com" target=_top>www.forthelost.com</a> <BR><a href="http://www.unsolved-crimes.com/" target=_top>http://www.unsolved-crimes.com/</a> <BR><a href="http://www.crimespider.com/cgi-bin/ilink/ilink.cgi?Category=Unsolved_Crimes" target=_top>http://www.crimespider.com/cgi-bin/ilink/ilink.cgi ?Category=Unsolved_Crimes</a>|Cold_Cases <BR><a href="http://coldcases.cjb.net/" target=_top>http://coldcases.cjb.net/</a> <BR><a href="http://www.projectedan.us/" target=_top>http://www.projectedan.us/</a> <BR><a href="http://nampn.doenetwork.us/" target=_top>http://nampn.doenetwork.us/</a> <BR> <BR>I have tons of links through my work, and I&#39;m comparing them to BTK when I have time.Perhaps you will find these useful...I have dozens more<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8746-->
<!--Post: 8753--><!--Time: 1109307086-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8753"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stormy74<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stormy74<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 8:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Weeza, <BR>Can you tell me if you have ran across any cold cases involving similar BTK MO&#39;s in Kansas City or areas surrounding KC? If so, would you mind posting the links you have found them on? Thank you. I will also be checking out those links you have provided. Thanks to you both for listing those links!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8753-->
<!--Post: 8756--><!--Time: 1109307870-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8756"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 9:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found one case in KC area last week, I&#39;ll see if I can dig it up<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8756-->
<!--Post: 8757--><!--Time: 1109308354-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8757"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 9:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.doenetwork.us/cases/6ufks.html" target=_top>http://www.doenetwork.us/cases/6ufks.html</a> <BR>That case is very vague and out of Ks state <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.doenetwork.us/cases/54ufmo.html" target=_top>http://www.doenetwork.us/cases/54ufmo.html</a> <BR>that case has the &#34;bind&#34; in BTK as part of it...but beheadings seem a little extreme for BTK. <BR> <BR>Give me some time and I&#39;ll dig up more <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8757-->
<!--Post: 8758--><!--Time: 1109309212-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8758"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 9:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m on page 10 of 46, with 30 cases per page, this may take awhile<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8758-->
<!--Post: 8765--><!--Time: 1109313684-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8765"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 10:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not too impressed with some of those sites, too fragmented to gain any real knowledge of what a string would look like. Also, when looking for similar mo and sig. NCIC has been available for years. It&#39;s the first tool LE uses to connect across jurisdictions. On one site they had a profile of &#34;Sidetrack&#34;, only they didn&#39;t even call him that. And they got the date of his arrest wrong by a year, and they credited him with 14 killings when he has confessed to either 37 or 38. I will say that one site showed a crime in 2003 in Colorado Springs that could show similar mo and sig to the Moulds killing. I don&#39;t have any doubt that BTK has not taken a long &#34;vacation&#34;, it&#39;s just that with the intel we have available to us, connecting the dots is pretty difficult when you don&#39;t know where the dots are.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8765-->
